Stubbs claimed "48-Hour waiting periods limit crimes of passion and keep our communities safe." Some studies have shown reductions in homicides in states with a waiting period, but many guns are obtained illegally or through sellers where background checks are not required. Meanwhile, "crimes of passion," by their very definition, happen in the moment, so if a gun were involved in such cases, the perpetrator would already have it. That said, studies show a waiting period can reduce suicides. So, there is some  for both parts of the , as well as factors that muddy the water. For a statement that is partially accurate but leaves out important details or takes things out of context, our rating is .   window.gciAnalyticsUAID = 'PMJS-TEALIUM-COBRAND';
